\tag{fdip}
\title{Chosen adjoints and parity}
\date{2026-10-20}

\p{Composition supplies a product on field operators. Two further
choices give it more structure: the counting pairing represents
adjoints, and a partition of the carrier separates even operators
from odd ones. Neither choice requires a positive coefficient field
or division by two.}

\p{The [four-cycle](fdip-001M) realizes both structures on actual
fields. Its shift is odd and invertible; over the integers its
difference operator has two nonzero parity components.
This distinguishes a graded operator
algebra from a complex with a square-zero differential before
specializing to [real paired differences](fdip-0016).}

